# Core AI stock arm on the Mac, v1 (2026-10-08; docs/coreai-arm-v1.md). Apple's own exports of the
# dashboard model set (apple/coreai-models bd3c539, its export pipeline unchanged, context 2048), run
# by Apple's static-shape engine on the stock path of the yardstick's CoreAIRuntime (llm-runner's call
# sequence). The engine pins chunked-static bundles to the Neural Engine; no public option picks the
# compute unit. backend=ane is arm identity only: rows stamp `core-ai-ane`, the runner passes nothing
# for it. The bundle fixes the KV allocation (the export's --max-context-length, the model id's
# -ctx2048); context-tokens=2048 names it, as the other arms' 1K rows name theirs.
#
# Two instruments per model, both arms:
#   long-context-1024-gen256  the 1K text task through the harness (the same prompt and record for
#                             every arm); runs=4 = run 1 cold, runs 2-4 warm (the Mac headline is warm)
#   native-benchmark-1024x256 each engine's own benchmark: Core AI = Apple's llm-benchmark
#                             measurement (yardstick --coreai-native-benchmark; runs=4 = 4 timed
#                             trials after the warmup trial, which is printed as trial 0, cold);
#                             LiteRT-LM = its benchmark() (yardstick --litert-native-benchmark;
#                             runs=4 = 4 calls in one process, call 1 cold)
# The two instruments count differently (docs/coreai-arm-v1.md "Record fields and definitions"),
# so their rows never pool. The LiteRT-LM rows are the same cells as
# matrices/dashboard-longctx1024-v1.cells and dashboard-protocol1024-v1.cells (same keys), here so
# that both arms run in one sitting: the same yardstick build, the same OS, the same hour.
# Native lines land in the cell's .jsonl (no schema-v1 record; build_summary skips them); lift them
# with scripts/import_native_benchmark.py --schema-v1 into <campaign>/app-path-native/
# (docs/coreai-arm-v1.md "Run one cell"). Bundles are staged under BENCH_COREAI_MODELS_DIR (default
# ~/.cache/edge-llm-bench/CoreAIModels/stock_<model>_ctx2048/); a missing one logs SKIPPED. The first
# load of a bundle under a yardstick's name specializes it (minutes for some bundles): specialize
# each bundle with one unmeasured launch before the sitting's cells (docs/coreai-arm-v1.md).
# Model order and cooldowns as matrices/dashboard-longctx1024-v1.cells; anchors = matrices/anchors.cells.
# Name the campaign <date>-dashboard-coreai-v1-<device>: the team dashboard reads only campaigns
# whose name contains "dashboard".
#   ./bench matrix matrices/dashboard-coreai-v1-mac.cells --platform mac --campaign <date>-dashboard-coreai-v1-m4max
#   scripts/bench_matrix_mac.sh run matrices/dashboard-coreai-v1-mac.cells --dry-run    # every row resolved, nothing run


# ---- session anchors ----
mac mlx-swift mlx-community/Qwen3-0.6B-4bit short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B short-chat anchor=1 runs=3

# --- Qwen3-0.6B ---
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-0.6b-stock-ctx2048 long-context-1024-gen256 backend=ane context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-0.6b-stock-ctx2048 native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=ane context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B long-context-1024-gen256 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048 runs=4

# --- Qwen3-1.7B ---
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-1.7b-stock-ctx2048 long-context-1024-gen256 backend=ane context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-1.7b-stock-ctx2048 native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=ane context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-1.7B long-context-1024-gen256 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-1.7B native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048 runs=4

# --- Gemma 4 E2B ---
mac core-ai core-ai/gemma4-e2b-stock-ctx2048 long-context-1024-gen256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac core-ai core-ai/gemma4-e2b-stock-ctx2048 native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm long-context-1024-gen256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4

# --- Qwen3-4B ---
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-4b-stock-ctx2048 long-context-1024-gen256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac core-ai core-ai/qwen3-4b-stock-ctx2048 native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-4B long-context-1024-gen256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-4B native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4

# --- Gemma 4 E4B --- (on the 1K text task Core AI's E4B ends its reply early, at the model's own
# end of turn: measured as it is, docs/coreai-arm-v1.md "Regime and disclosure"; its native row
# decodes 256)
mac core-ai core-ai/gemma4-e4b-stock-ctx2048 long-context-1024-gen256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac core-ai core-ai/gemma4-e4b-stock-ctx2048 native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=ane cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E4B-it-litert-lm long-context-1024-gen256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E4B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048 runs=4
